@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `law08-vintage`
IMPORT `law08-nouns`
IMPORT `law08-ch2-general`

-- Chuong II, Muc 3 (Dieu 43-56) property and damage contracts, and Muc 4 (Dieu 57-61) liability
-- contracts. Law 139/2025/QH15 does not touch these articles: one arm each. Where a rule has the
-- Law's "tuong ung" (corresponding) without a formula, the proportion taken is stated in the rule and
-- in the fork register (F21, F22). Amounts are VND.

§ `Chuong II, Muc 3: Hop dong bao hiem tai san, hop dong bao hiem thiet hai`

§§ `Dieu 43: the object of insurance`

@@q 897 901
@ref Dieu 43 (src:897-901)
GIVEN c IS A `A class of insurance contract`
GIVETH A `An object of insurance`
`Dieu 43: the object of insurance of a property or damage contract` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `a property insurance contract` THEN `property as the Civil Code defines it`
    WHEN `a damage insurance contract`   THEN `an economic interest or an obligation under a contract or by law that the insured person bears on a loss`
    OTHERWISE REFUSE "Dieu 43 governs property and damage contracts only; Dieu 33 and Dieu 57 govern the other classes"

§§ `Dieu 44: insurable interest`

@@q 904 906
@ref Dieu 44 (src:904-906)
GIVEN l IS A `A property or damage contract and a loss`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 44(1): the policyholder has an insurable interest in the insured property` l MEANS
    l's `the policyholder is owner, holds another right in the property or possesses or uses it without owning`

@@q 907 909
@ref Dieu 44 (src:907-909)
GIVEN l IS A `A property or damage contract and a loss`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 44(2): the policyholder has an insurable interest in the damage` l MEANS
    l's `the policyholder has a financial interest, financial obligation or liability, or economic loss in respect of the object`

-- Dieu 44(3). At the time of the loss the policyholder or the insured person must have it.
@@q 910 911
@ref Dieu 44 (src:910-911)
GIVEN l IS A `A property or damage contract and a loss`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 44(3): the insurable interest exists at the time of the loss` l MEANS
    l's `the policyholder or insured person has the insurable interest at the time of the loss`

§§ `Dieu 45: the sum insured`

@@q 913 916
@ref Dieu 45 (src:913-916)
`Dieu 45 — the sum insured is the sum the policyholder and the insurer agree in the contract to insure property and damage on the policyholder's request (a definition; the sum insured is an input field of the contract)` MEANS
    "An agreed figure, not computed by the Law."

§§ `Dieu 46: notice of the insured event`

-- Dieu 46(1). If the policyholder fails or is late to notify the insurer within the time the contract
-- agrees, the insurer may reduce the compensation by the loss it bears because of that, unless force
-- majeure or an objective obstacle. Dieu 46(2): the insurer may not do so if the contract does not agree the
-- policyholder's responsibility and the sanctions for failing or delaying the notice.
@@q 918 932
@ref Dieu 46 (src:918-932)
GIVEN n IS A `A notice of the insured event`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 46: the insurer may reduce the compensation` n MEANS
        (NOT n's `the policyholder notified within the time the contract agrees`)
    AND (NOT n's `force majeure or an objective obstacle prevented timely notice`)
    AND n's `the contract agrees the policyholder's responsibility and the sanctions for failing or delaying to notify`

GIVEN n IS A `A notice of the insured event`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Dieu 46: the compensation after the reduction` n MEANS
    IF `Dieu 46: the insurer may reduce the compensation` n
    THEN max 0 (n's `compensation otherwise payable` MINUS n's `the loss the insurer bears because of the failure or delay`)
    ELSE n's `compensation otherwise payable`

§§ `Dieu 47: insurance above value`

-- Dieu 47(1). The sum insured is higher than the market value at the time of making. The insurer and the
-- policyholder may not make such a contract deliberately.
@@q 934 938
@ref Dieu 47 (src:934-938)
GIVEN l IS A `A property or damage contract and a loss`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 47(1): the contract insures above value` l MEANS
    l's `sum insured` ABOVE l's `market value of the property at the time of making`

GIVEN l IS A `A property or damage contract and a loss`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 47(1): the making of the contract is prohibited` l MEANS
    `Dieu 47(1): the contract insures above value` l AND l's `the over-insurance was made deliberately`

-- Dieu 47(2)(a). Unintentional over-insurance, before an insured event: the insurer refunds the premium
-- paid "tuong ung" with the excess of the sum insured over the market value at the time of making, less the
-- reasonable costs the contract allows. The proportion taken is premium x excess / sum insured (F21).
@@q 939 945
@ref Dieu 47 (src:939-945)
GIVEN l IS A `A property or damage contract and a loss`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Dieu 47(2): the premium the insurer must refund` l MEANS
    IF NOT (`Dieu 47(1): the contract insures above value` l AND l's `the over-insurance was made through the policyholder's unintentional fault`)
    THEN REFUSE "Dieu 47(2) applies to an over-insurance made through the policyholder's unintentional fault"
    ELSE IF `the proportionate premium for the excess` l AT LEAST l's `reasonable costs the contract allows to be deducted`
         THEN `the proportionate premium for the excess` l MINUS l's `reasonable costs the contract allows to be deducted`
         ELSE REFUSE "Dieu 47(2) says nothing on reasonable costs above the premium for the excess"

GIVEN l IS A `A property or damage contract and a loss`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the proportionate premium for the excess` l MEANS
    l's `premium paid` TIMES (l's `sum insured` MINUS l's `market value of the property at the time of making`) DIVIDED BY l's `sum insured`

-- Dieu 47(2)(b). After an insured event the insurer pays only the loss "tuong ung" with the market value at
-- the time of the loss, which is read as: no more than that market value (F22); the premium refund is the same.
@@q 946 952
@ref Dieu 47 (src:946-952)
GIVEN l IS A `A property or damage contract and a loss`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Dieu 47(2)(b): the compensation for the loss` l MEANS
    IF NOT (`Dieu 47(1): the contract insures above value` l AND l's `the over-insurance was made through the policyholder's unintentional fault` AND l's `the insured event has occurred`)
    THEN REFUSE "Dieu 47(2)(b) applies to an unintentional over-insurance after the insured event"
    ELSE min (l's `actual loss`) (l's `market value of the property at the time and place of the loss`)

§§ `Dieu 48: insurance below value`

-- Dieu 48. The sum insured is lower than the market value at the time of making; the insurer pays the loss
-- in the proportion of the sum insured to that market value, or as the contract agrees.
@@q 956 963
@ref Dieu 48 (src:956-963)
GIVEN l IS A `A property or damage contract and a loss`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 48(1): the contract insures below value` l MEANS
    l's `sum insured` BELOW l's `market value of the property at the time of making`

GIVEN l IS A `A property or damage contract and a loss`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Dieu 48(2): the compensation for the loss` l MEANS
    IF NOT `Dieu 48(1): the contract insures below value` l
    THEN REFUSE "Dieu 48(2) applies to a contract insuring below value"
    ELSE IF l's `the contract agrees otherwise on compensation`
         THEN REFUSE "Dieu 48(2): the contract agrees otherwise and the Law does not give the agreed amount"
         ELSE l's `actual loss` TIMES l's `sum insured` DIVIDED BY l's `market value of the property at the time of making`

§§ `Dieu 49: double insurance`

-- Dieu 49(1)-(2). Two or more contracts for the same scope, object, term and insured event, with a total
-- sum insured above the market value at the time of making. Each contract pays in the ratio of its sum
-- insured to the total; the total paid does not exceed the actual loss.
@@q 965 973
@ref Dieu 49 (src:965-973)
GIVEN d IS A `A double insurance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 49(1): the contracts are in double insurance` d MEANS
        count (d's `contracts`) AT LEAST 2
    AND d's `the contracts cover the same scope, object, term and insured event`
    AND `the total sum insured` d ABOVE d's `market value of the property at the time of making`

GIVEN d IS A `A double insurance`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the total sum insured` d MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN c YIELD c's `sum insured`) (d's `contracts`))

GIVEN d IS A `A double insurance`
      c IS A `A contract in a double insurance`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Dieu 49(2): the compensation under the contract` d c MEANS
    IF `Dieu 49(1): the contracts are in double insurance` d
    THEN d's `actual loss` TIMES c's `sum insured` DIVIDED BY `the total sum insured` d
    ELSE REFUSE "Dieu 49(2) applies to contracts in double insurance as Dieu 49(1) defines it"

§§ `Dieu 50: wear and tear and inherent nature`

@@q 975 978
@ref Dieu 50 (src:975-978)
GIVEN l IS A `A property or damage contract and a loss`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 50: the insurer is not liable for the loss` l MEANS
    l's `the loss is natural wear and tear or the inherent nature of the property` AND (NOT l's `the contract agrees otherwise on compensation`)

§§ `Dieu 51: the basis of compensation`

-- Dieu 51(1)-(2). The compensation rests on the market value at the time and place of the loss and on the
-- actual extent of the damage, and does not exceed the sum insured, unless the contract agrees otherwise.
-- The actual loss field is the loss so valued. Dieu 51(3): the insurer also pays the necessary and reasonable
-- costs of preventing and limiting loss, and the costs incurred in following its instructions.
@@q 980 996
@ref Dieu 51 (src:980-996)
GIVEN l IS A `A property or damage contract and a loss`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Dieu 51(1)-(2): the compensation` l MEANS
    IF l's `the contract agrees otherwise on compensation`
    THEN REFUSE "Dieu 51: the contract agrees otherwise and the Law does not give the agreed basis"
    ELSE min (l's `actual loss`) (l's `sum insured`)

GIVEN l IS A `A property or damage contract and a loss`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Dieu 51(3): the costs the insurer must pay besides the compensation` l MEANS
    l's `costs reasonably and necessarily incurred to prevent and limit the loss` PLUS l's `costs the policyholder or insured person incurred in following the insurer's instructions`

§§ `Dieu 52: the form of compensation`

@@q 998 1006
@ref Dieu 52 (src:998-1006)
GIVEN f IS A `A form agreed for compensation`
GIVETH A `A form of compensation`
`Dieu 52: the form of compensation` f MEANS
    CONSIDER f's `form agreed`
    WHEN JUST x THEN x
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `payment of compensation in money`

-- Dieu 52(3). For replacement or payment, the insurer may take the damaged property once it has replaced it
-- or compensated in full at market value.
@@q 1007 1010
@ref Dieu 52 (src:1007-1010)
GIVEN f IS A `A form agreed for compensation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 52(3): the insurer may recover the damaged property` f MEANS
        (NOT (`Dieu 52: the form of compensation` f EQUALS `repair of the damaged property`))
    AND f's `the damaged property was replaced or fully compensated at market value`

§§ `Dieu 53: loss adjustment`

@@q 1012 1025
@ref Dieu 53 (src:1012-1025)
GIVEN a IS A `A loss adjustment and recourse`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 53(2): the parties may agree to hire an independent loss adjuster` a MEANS
    (NOT a's `the parties agree on the cause and extent of the loss`) AND (NOT a's `the contract provides otherwise`)

GIVEN a IS A `A loss adjustment and recourse`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 53(2): a party may ask the court or arbitration to obtain an independent loss adjuster` a MEANS
        `Dieu 53(2): the parties may agree to hire an independent loss adjuster` a
    AND (NOT a's `the parties agreed to hire an independent loss adjuster`)

§§ `Dieu 54: transferring the right to claim reimbursement`

@@q 1027 1037
@ref Dieu 54 (src:1027-1037)
GIVEN a IS A `A loss adjustment and recourse`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 54(1)(a): the insured person must transfer the right to claim reimbursement` a MEANS
    a's `a third person is liable for the loss` AND a's `compensation paid` ABOVE 0

-- Dieu 54(1)(b). If the insured person refuses, the insurer may deduct from the compensation according to the
-- insured person's degree of fault; the Law gives no formula for the amount.
GIVEN a IS A `A loss adjustment and recourse`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 54(1)(b): the insurer may deduct from the compensation` a MEANS
    `Dieu 54(1)(a): the insured person must transfer the right to claim reimbursement` a AND a's `the insured person refused to transfer the right to claim against the third person`

GIVEN a IS A `A loss adjustment and recourse`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Dieu 54(1)(b): the amount the insurer may deduct` a MEANS
    REFUSE "Dieu 54(1)(b) says the deduction depends on the insured person's degree of fault but gives no formula"

@@q 1043 1049
@ref Dieu 54 (src:1043-1049)
GIVEN a IS A `A loss adjustment and recourse`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 54(3): the insurer may claim reimbursement from the third person` a MEANS
    a's `a third person is liable for the loss` AND ((NOT a's `the third person is the insured person's parent, spouse or child`) OR a's `that person deliberately caused the loss`)

§§ `Dieu 55: safety rules`

@@q 1051 1053
@ref Dieu 55 (src:1051-1053)
`Dieu 55(1)-(2) — the insured person must observe fire prevention, labour safety and hygiene and other safety rules; the insurer may inspect safety conditions and recommend or require risk measures (duties and powers stated; the breach of 55(1) is tested by 55(3))` MEANS
    "The insured person observes the safety rules; the insurer may inspect and require measures."

@@q 1058 1064
@ref Dieu 55 (src:1058-1064)
GIVEN s IS A `A safety measure`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 55(3): the insurer may raise the premium or terminate the contract` s MEANS
    s's `the insured person failed to take the safety measures` AND s's `the insurer fixed a time for taking them` AND s's `the time has expired and they are still not taken`

§§ `Dieu 56: no abandonment of the insured property`

@@q 1066 1069
@ref Dieu 56 (src:1066-1069)
GIVEN `the law provides otherwise or the parties agreed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 56: the insured person may abandon the insured property` `the law provides otherwise or the parties agreed otherwise` MEANS
    `the law provides otherwise or the parties agreed otherwise`

§ `Chuong II, Muc 4: Hop dong bao hiem trach nhiem`

§§ `Dieu 57: the object of insurance`

@@q 1077 1078
@ref Dieu 57 (src:1077-1078)
GIVEN c IS A `A class of insurance contract`
GIVETH A `An object of insurance`
`Dieu 57: the object of insurance of a liability contract` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `a liability insurance contract` THEN `the civil liability of the insured person to a third person under the law`
    OTHERWISE REFUSE "Dieu 57 governs liability contracts only; Dieu 33 and Dieu 43 govern the other classes"

§§ `Dieu 58: the insurer's liability`

@@q 1083 1089
@ref Dieu 58 (src:1083-1089)
GIVEN l IS A `A liability contract and a claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 58(1): the insurer's liability arises` l MEANS
    l's `a third person claimed compensation from the insured person` AND l's `the act causing the damage occurred within the insurance term`

-- Dieu 58(1) can be read the other way (fork F27): "trong thoi han bao hiem" ("within the insurance term") may qualify the
-- third person's claim (a claims-made reading) rather than the act that caused the damage (an occurrence reading, above).
GIVEN l IS A `A liability contract and a claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 58(1): the insurer's liability arises (claims-made reading)` l MEANS
    l's `a third person claimed compensation from the insured person` AND l's `the third person's claim was made within the insurance term`

GIVEN l IS A `A liability contract and a claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 58(2): the third person may claim directly from the insurer` l MEANS
    l's `the law provides that the third person may claim directly`

§§ `Dieu 59: the limit of liability`

@@q 1091 1107
@ref Dieu 59 (src:1091-1107)
GIVEN l IS A `A liability contract and a claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Dieu 59(2)-(4): the total the insurer pays` l MEANS
    IF NOT `Dieu 58(1): the insurer's liability arises` l
    THEN REFUSE "Dieu 58(1): the insurer's liability has not arisen"
    ELSE IF l's `the contract agrees otherwise on the limit`
         THEN REFUSE "Dieu 59(4): the contract agrees otherwise on the limit and the Law does not give the agreed total"
         ELSE min (l's `limit of liability`) (l's `amount the insured person must pay the third person by law` PLUS l's `costs of resolving the dispute on liability to the third person` PLUS l's `interest payable to the third person for the insured person's late payment as the insurer directed`)

@@q 1108 1115
@ref Dieu 59 (src:1108-1115)
GIVEN l IS A `A liability contract and a claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 59(5): the insurer must give the bond or deposit` l MEANS
        l's `the insured person must post a bond or deposit to keep the property from detention or to avoid a suit`
    AND l's `the insured person asks the insurer to give the bond or deposit`
    AND l's `the contract so agrees`

§§ `Dieu 60: representing the insured person`

@@q 1117 1120
@ref Dieu 60 (src:1117-1120)
GIVEN l IS A `A liability contract and a claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 60: the insurer may negotiate for the insured person` l MEANS
    NOT l's `the contract agrees otherwise on representation`

§§ `Dieu 61: the way of compensating`

@@q 1122 1124
@ref Dieu 61 (src:1122-1124)
GIVEN `the insured person asks for direct payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 61: the insurer may compensate the insured person directly or the damaged third person` `the insured person asks for direct payment` MEANS
    `the insured person asks for direct payment`
